# The build happens INSIDE the image, so the context carries SOURCE and nothing else.
# This file is a correctness boundary, not hygiene: the first two entries would poison
# the build rather than merely slow it.

# Host-specific and actively harmful. `.cargo/config.toml` names this machine's
# interpreter by absolute path (PYTHONHOME, an rpath into a host-only uv install), and
# the venvs are symlink farms pointing into it. Copied in, they do not fail loudly —
# they can produce a build that succeeds while pointing pyo3 at an interpreter that
# cannot `import goofi`, which drops every Python node to the subprocess tier silently.
.cargo/config.toml
.gfivenv/
.gfivenv-ft/

# Build outputs, all regenerated inside. `target/` alone is ~23 GB on a working clone
# (cargo never garbage-collects it), which is the difference between a context that
# transfers in a second and one that does not.
target/
frontend/build/
frontend/node_modules/
tests/e2e/node_modules/
node_modules/
.svelte-kit/

# Not inputs to a build.
.git/
.github/
docs/
crates/
*.gfi
